{"id":"bp08","name":"Invert the Score Mapping","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["legacy"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>An old scoring system stores its configuration as a dictionary <code>legacy</code> where each key is a score (written as a string) and each value is the list of upper-case letters that are worth this score.</p>\n<p>The new system needs the opposite mapping. Your task is to return a dictionary where each key is a letter in <b>lower case</b> and each value is its score as an <b>integer</b>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p><code>legacy = {\"1\": [\"A\", \"E\"], \"2\": [\"D\"], \"10\": [\"Q\", \"Z\"]}</code></p><p>the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">{\"a\": 1, \"e\": 1, \"d\": 2, \"q\": 10, \"z\": 10}</pre><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> dictionary legacy<br><b>[output]</b> dictionary</div>","starter":"def solution(legacy):\n    # write your code here\n    return {}\n","hints":["Deux boucles : pour chaque score, pour chaque lettre, out[lettre.lower()] = int(score)."],"summary_fr":"Inverser une table {score: [lettres]} en {lettre en minuscule: score} (le score devient un entier).","tags":["dict","inverser une table","minuscules"],"minutes":8,"source":"exercism/problem-specifications (MIT) · etl","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"legacy":{"1":["A","E"],"2":["D"],"10":["Q","Z"]}},"expected":{"value":{"a":1,"e":1,"d":2,"q":10,"z":10}}},{"input":{"legacy":{"4":["F","H"],"8":["J"]}},"expected":{"value":{"f":4,"h":4,"j":8}}}],"hidden_n":5,"hidden":"","solution":"ImRlZiBzb2x1dGlvbihsZWdhY3kpOlxuICAgIG91dCA9IHt9XG4gICAgZm9yIHNjb3JlLCBsZXR0ZXJzIGluIGxlZ2FjeS5pdGVtcygpOlxuICAgICAgICBmb3IgbGV0dGVyIGluIGxldHRlcnM6XG4gICAgICAgICAgICBvdXRbbGV0dGVyLmxvd2VyKCldID0gaW50KHNjb3JlKVxuICAgIHJldHVybiBvdXRcbiI="}